{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_5e96aa5359af4896b06dbbf40889ae81","id":"pg_5752cb8334bc5792b17cecfbf76ea67e","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/qwen-code-dev-bot-oh-my-cli-security-md-8dce0123dabf-ecfbf76ea67e.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_778f6f6bac5f52529ffaa43457b55efa"],"title":"qwen-code-dev-bot/oh-my-cli/SECURITY.md @ 8dce0123dabf","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5e96aa5359af4896b06dbbf40889ae81"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_092106189ce2baae2f059c1d1d8c7a7f2ead208cc4ff0564bd4828525dd52ab7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Compaction writes a versioned summary sidecar validated against the transcript digest before use, keeping completed tool actions as redacted receipts the resumed model is told not to repeat."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0f0a4d28d856fd5f60a1cbf94b9f37c35aa418d7309544e6b14e1abb6f7a9f2c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Folder trust is a fail-closed top-level boundary: workspaces are untrusted by default, trust is recorded in a user-owned store a project cannot write, and approval modes are subordinate to it."},{"claim_ids":["clm_10cbbcb9bcd171f47eccb713cb1e6d14f4a48bbc6c372e46e5f9ad04f6813438"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Three approval modes exist: default prompts for every mutating tool and denies without a TTY, auto-edit allows write/edit but still prompts for shell, and yolo allows all tools without prompting; read operations never require approval."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1650f165fb9b0cfeed6dce694fccc83d6405b3c18e62fb04fd4f99c09664441a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors install with npm install, npm run build, and npm link (or invoke node dist/index.js), and are pointed to a first-run guide with a --doctor setup check."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1ad7d991a2c594d6c88b93602ec36c27c33fd6e9870780bd83189f8a1a1ba4d8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Trust enforcement is opt-in via --enforce-folder-trust or OMC_ENFORCE_FOLDER_TRUST=1; trust states include trusted, sandbox-enforced, untrusted, and sandbox-unavailable, with mutation denied in the latter two."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3139133b998a08d66cb7a73dd18541ca5d94999b7dd8b7ebf83937e888cd6319"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Model configuration resolves from environment variables, an optional trusted workspace .env, and a user settings file, with environment variables taking highest precedence; raw credential fields like model.apiKey are rejected in favor of apiKeyEnv references."},{"claim_ids":["clm_34a3cebc5dfe9ac5c68ca8b4381dfc5e091aba20b4b4668e2b401fb3b1f12aff"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Undo/redo of a completed turn uses content-based checkpoints of only the files the turn's mutating tools touched, restoring pre-images without git reset, and fails closed (exit 2) if files diverged."},{"claim_ids":["clm_35bd6a4b4f60cca6240187e0adb17f53db053376f5dafd6c239d87900806c56a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Session-targeted flags (--resume, --session-stats, --tasks, --export-session, --compact, --undo-turn, --redo-turn, --session) accept an exact id or user-owned name and fail closed on ambiguous, corrupt, or unknown values."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4696e232862a3ec2e1c35f3bd6403883afe60ae3aff6bbba54888ad71ad8722e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Named model profiles can be declared in the user settings file and selected via --profile, --list-profiles, or a defaultProfile, with project-local settings files unable to set profiles."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4ba1e3cf6dbd27990927fa465a83787fa952c28862ba80aabdca071a78446048"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is built with Node.js 22, TypeScript, and ESM, and is installed via npm install/build/link or by running the built dist/index.js directly."},{"claim_ids":["clm_618bcd1772bc99379ea6217b080ee79415ed9d7a369bc2dd67c9720c1d4867c7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A --delivery-web command serves a loopback-only web delivery board (default port 4317, configurable via --web-port) with /remote-control and /dynamic-workflow pages that expose no credentials or file server."},{"claim_ids":["clm_66517b652e54c27eea6295c96ccf87f50a372adfe4f36248de6006e56f1574d9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Workspace .env loading is gated by folder trust, parsed only for model-config resolution without mutating process.env, and .env.local/.env.production variants and nested .env files are not read."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7c3c9b8f0f7f190911a5d54e28196bb82bf3b6a77681d8df574b077c6a0532dc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sessions persist as JSONL under ~/.oh-my-cli/sessions/ with atomic checkpointing; on resume, complete checkpoints are promoted, partial ones discarded, and corrupt ones quarantined rather than deleted."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8dc6e19137cd8c607b258edf77dd7cbfc6973695bf82e1277368dddb4b8d9dfb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Approval previews and command-policy denials neutralize spoofing Unicode (bidi controls, zero-width characters, look-alike quotes) by replacing each with a visible [U+XXXX] marker to prevent Trojan Source-style disguise."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a44269fa06978844121d5cd4af43abf3b00df667ad3efcf951e187d49654b506"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Side questions answer clarifications against a bounded read-only session snapshot with tool execution and workspace mutation structurally disabled, leaving the source session byte-identical."},{"claim_ids":["clm_abee26576b49a4b2e3c0b250c106359835e7cda9a9a04ae4f57a0eea4aaab717"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"With --output json and -p, the CLI emits a versioned newline-delimited JSON event stream (protocol oh-my-cli.headless) with start, assistant, tool_start, tool_result, usage, retry, error, and complete records."},{"claim_ids":["clm_acb39ede77441a53dbf584003f465dc20f2ae13dc19235d97d811d2e569500a5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"oh-my-cli is a small self-hosted code agent CLI that reads and edits files and runs shell commands under a safety plane, against any OpenAI-compatible endpoint."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ae480fb18081c8b6e3e1af5c1f743db1d99be70ac5b73fd92b290a1f7503ddc8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project targets terminal-based code-agent workflows with headless CI automation, spend budgets, and an Electron desktop shell, and is Apache-2.0 licensed with contribution and security policies."},{"claim_ids":["clm_df8d09fa449e52ec1c323fb4989c5c0a9c2f45a29ad6ce3580be5b998409724b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI offers run summaries and scorecards: --summary emits metadata-only outcome/exit/reason/token/cost data, and --baseline/--candidate compare two summary files captured via --summary-out."}],"claim_ids":["clm_092106189ce2baae2f059c1d1d8c7a7f2ead208cc4ff0564bd4828525dd52ab7","clm_0f0a4d28d856fd5f60a1cbf94b9f37c35aa418d7309544e6b14e1abb6f7a9f2c","clm_10cbbcb9bcd171f47eccb713cb1e6d14f4a48bbc6c372e46e5f9ad04f6813438","clm_1650f165fb9b0cfeed6dce694fccc83d6405b3c18e62fb04fd4f99c09664441a","clm_1ad7d991a2c594d6c88b93602ec36c27c33fd6e9870780bd83189f8a1a1ba4d8","clm_3139133b998a08d66cb7a73dd18541ca5d94999b7dd8b7ebf83937e888cd6319","clm_34a3cebc5dfe9ac5c68ca8b4381dfc5e091aba20b4b4668e2b401fb3b1f12aff","clm_35bd6a4b4f60cca6240187e0adb17f53db053376f5dafd6c239d87900806c56a","clm_4696e232862a3ec2e1c35f3bd6403883afe60ae3aff6bbba54888ad71ad8722e","clm_4ba1e3cf6dbd27990927fa465a83787fa952c28862ba80aabdca071a78446048","clm_618bcd1772bc99379ea6217b080ee79415ed9d7a369bc2dd67c9720c1d4867c7","clm_66517b652e54c27eea6295c96ccf87f50a372adfe4f36248de6006e56f1574d9","clm_7c3c9b8f0f7f190911a5d54e28196bb82bf3b6a77681d8df574b077c6a0532dc","clm_8dc6e19137cd8c607b258edf77dd7cbfc6973695bf82e1277368dddb4b8d9dfb","clm_a44269fa06978844121d5cd4af43abf3b00df667ad3efcf951e187d49654b506","clm_abee26576b49a4b2e3c0b250c106359835e7cda9a9a04ae4f57a0eea4aaab717","clm_acb39ede77441a53dbf584003f465dc20f2ae13dc19235d97d811d2e569500a5","clm_ae480fb18081c8b6e3e1af5c1f743db1d99be70ac5b73fd92b290a1f7503ddc8","clm_df8d09fa449e52ec1c323fb4989c5c0a9c2f45a29ad6ce3580be5b998409724b"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_5e96aa5359af4896b06dbbf40889ae81","id":"pg_633343bdce685292ae50d31abed1da08","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/qwen-code-dev-bot-oh-my-cli-readme-md-8dce0123dabf-d31abed1da08.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_850d525e7a915e2ab622ed96e9291910"],"title":"qwen-code-dev-bot/oh-my-cli/README.md @ 8dce0123dabf","updated_at":"